WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 8.2 · Marketing & Communications
Audiences and segmentation

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Group the people you need by what they need from you, and give each group a priority.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.022
Audiences are the groups of people you need to reach. Segmenting means splitting a broad audience where needs differ, so the little time you have goes to the people your launch depends on.

4
00:00:27.422 --> 00:00:28.022
From broad to specific

5
00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:40.093
Broad audiences: Grouped from your stakeholder map by what they need and what you need from them. For example: For our bakery: neighbours, market shoppers, cafés, the youth centre and small funders.

6
00:00:40.093 --> 00:00:50.311
Segments: Splits within an audience where needs differ, each given a priority. For example: Regulars who come every Saturday; cautious shoppers who want a taste first.

7
00:00:50.311 --> 00:01:03.581
Persona: A short portrait of a typical member of a segment, drawn from real conversations. For example: María, 64, buys bread every Saturday, distrusts apps and hears news at the market.

8
00:01:03.981 --> 00:01:04.581
Why it matters

9
00:01:04.581 --> 00:01:09.144
1. Different people need different messages before they act.

10
00:01:09.144 --> 00:01:13.707
2. Priorities stop you spreading your time too thin.

11
00:01:13.707 --> 00:01:19.270
3. Personas from real conversations replace guesses and stereotypes.

12
00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:20.270
What it guides

13
00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:25.204
1. Your messaging framework: a version for each priority audience.

14
00:01:25.204 --> 00:01:30.137
2. Your channel choices: where each segment already spends time.

15
00:01:30.137 --> 00:01:34.959
3. Your campaigns: one audience, one action.

16
00:01:35.359 --> 00:01:35.959
What to avoid

17
00:01:35.959 --> 00:01:38.670
Writing for “everyone”.

18
00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:43.233
Building personas from stereotypes or your own guesses.

19
00:01:43.233 --> 00:01:49.167
Not noting how many people you actually spoke to.

20
00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:51.567
You define priority segments and write one persona.

21
00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:55.567
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:01:57.067 --> 00:02:00.167
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
